body:
@zzzeek Personally I don't think that the proxy solution is a great fit for the async objects here, unless we suggest to use `sync_engine`/`sync_session`, with the relates problems (eg `sync_session.commit()` will not work/raise exceptions).
It's easy for bug like these to happen and it requires a lot of duplication.

Maybe a `BaseEngine`/`BaseSession` to be used as base classes for both the sync and async version with the common code would be the best solution?
